  "sections": [
    {
      "title": "Network Policies: What and Why",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 0,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Network Policies: What and Why",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Default and Definition",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Default is ==allow-all==: every pod reaches every pod, in any namespace",
                "{red:No policy} = no restriction",
                "A NetworkPolicy is a ==namespaced allow-list firewall==",
                "Works at **L3/L4**: IP, port, protocol",
                "Applies to pods chosen by a ==selector=="
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Additive and Allow-Only",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Policies only **allow**; there are no deny rules",
                "Policies are ==additive==: the union of all allows applies",
                "Once any policy selects a pod, unmatched traffic is {red:dropped} for that direction",
                "Policies are ==stateful==: replies to allowed connections pass automatically"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Pod state",
                "Result"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Selected by no policy",
                  "All traffic open"
                ],
                [
                  "Selected, `Ingress` listed",
                  "Only listed inbound allowed"
                ],
                [
                  "Selected, `Egress` not listed",
                  "Outbound still open"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Isolation per Direction",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Pod is isolated for ingress or egress only if a selecting policy lists that ==policyType==",
                "Unselected pods stay open"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "yaml",
              "lines": [
                "kind: NetworkPolicy",
                "spec:",
                "  podSelector:",
                "    matchLabels: {app: api}",
                "  policyTypes: [Ingress]"
              ],
              "note": "api pods: inbound isolated, outbound still open"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "Isolation is ==per direction==, and a policy can only add allows, never deny."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Selectors and Rule Anatomy",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Selectors and Rule Anatomy",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. What the policy protects",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`spec.podSelector` picks the pods the policy ==protects==",
                "`podSelector: {}` selects ==every pod== in the policy's namespace"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Rule peers in from / to",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Peer",
                "Matches",
                "Scope"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`podSelector`",
                  "pod labels",
                  "{green:same namespace}"
                ],
                [
                  "`namespaceSelector`",
                  "namespace labels; label it first, `kubernetes.io/metadata.name` is automatic",
                  "other namespaces"
                ],
                [
                  "`ipBlock`",
                  "CIDR, optional `except`",
                  "IP ranges"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Example: frontend to api",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Protect `app=api`, allow `app=frontend` on ==TCP 8080== only"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "yaml",
              "lines": [
                "spec:",
                "  podSelector:",
                "    matchLabels: {app: api}",
                "  ingress:",
                "  - from:",
                "    - podSelector:",
                "        matchLabels: {app: frontend}",
                "    ports: [{protocol: TCP, port: 8080}]"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. AND vs OR",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "One dash flips it",
              "text": "Both selectors in ==one item== = **AND**. Two separate items = **OR**, far wider. A missing dash flips the meaning."
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "yaml",
              "lines": [
                "# AND: one item",
                "- namespaceSelector: {matchLabels: {team: a}}",
                "  podSelector: {matchLabels: {app: web}}",
                "# OR: two items",
                "- namespaceSelector: {matchLabels: {team: a}}",
                "- podSelector: {matchLabels: {app: web}}"
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Ingress and Egress Rules",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Ingress and Egress Rules",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. policyTypes",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "policyTypes",
                "Controls",
                "Peers via"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`Ingress`",
                  "inbound to selected pods",
                  "`from`"
                ],
                [
                  "`Egress`",
                  "outbound from selected pods",
                  "`to`"
                ],
                [
                  "both listed",
                  "both directions",
                  "`from` + `to`"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Omitted ==policyTypes== defaults to `Ingress`",
                "`Egress` is added only if the policy has an `egress` section"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Two Checks per Connection",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Source pod",
                    "sub": "egress checked here",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Destination pod",
                    "sub": "ingress checked here",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Connected",
                    "sub": "both allowed",
                    "ink": "green"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. from, to and ports",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "yaml",
              "lines": [
                "ingress:",
                "- from:",
                "  - podSelector: {matchLabels: {app: web}}",
                "  - ipBlock: {cidr: 10.0.0.0/8}",
                "  ports:",
                "  - {protocol: TCP, port: 8080}"
              ],
              "note": "two peers = OR; ports limit both"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Entries in `from` / `to` are ==ORed==",
                "`ports` restricts which ports apply to those peers",
                "Omit `from` / `to`, keep `ports`: ==all peers== on those ports"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Both ends needed",
              "text": "Egress allowed at the source but no ingress on the target (or vice versa): traffic ==still drops==."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Default Deny and DNS Egress",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 3,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Default Deny and DNS Egress",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Default deny",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Empty `podSelector` + `policyTypes` + {red:no rules} = ==deny all==",
                "Start with deny all, then add allow policies per app"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Goal",
                "policyTypes",
                "Blocks"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Deny ingress",
                  "`[Ingress]`",
                  "all inbound"
                ],
                [
                  "Deny egress",
                  "`[Egress]`",
                  "all outbound, ==DNS too=="
                ],
                [
                  "Deny all",
                  "`[Ingress, Egress]`",
                  "both"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "yaml",
              "lines": [
                "apiVersion: networking.k8s.io/v1",
                "kind: NetworkPolicy",
                "metadata: {name: default-deny-all}",
                "spec:",
                "  podSelector: {}",
                "  policyTypes: [Ingress, Egress]"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Allow DNS egress",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Target: kube-system pods ==k8s-app=kube-dns==",
                "One list item = namespaceSelector AND podSelector",
                "Port ==53== on both {blue:UDP} and {blue:TCP}",
                "Extra policy: allows are additive"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "yaml",
              "lines": [
                "metadata: {name: allow-dns}",
                "spec:",
                "  podSelector: {}",
                "  policyTypes: [Egress]",
                "  egress:",
                "  - to: [{namespaceSelector: {matchLabels: {kubernetes.io/metadata.name: kube-system}}, podSelector: {matchLabels: {k8s-app: kube-dns}}}]",
                "    ports: [{protocol: UDP, port: 53}, {protocol: TCP, port: 53}]"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Mistake: egress deny, no DNS allow",
              "text": "Service names fail to resolve. Pod IPs allowed by another egress rule still work; with no allow, IPs drop too."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "CNI Support and Testing Policies",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 4,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "CNI Support and Testing Policies",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Who enforces policies",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "The ==CNI plugin== enforces NetworkPolicy, **not** the API server",
                "{green:Enforce it}: Calico, Cilium, Weave Net",
                "{red:Flannel alone}: objects accepted, then silently ignored"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "False security",
              "text": "On Flannel alone `kubectl apply` succeeds and nothing is blocked. ==Check the CNI== before trusting a policy."
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Test with a throwaway pod",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "bash",
              "lines": [
                "kubectl run test --rm -it --image=busybox -- \\",
                "  wget -qO- --timeout=2 http://svc:8080"
              ],
              "note": "timeout 2s: a blocked connection fails fast instead of hanging"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Run from",
                "Expect"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Pod with the {green:permitted label}",
                  "Response returned"
                ],
                [
                  "Pod {red:without} the label",
                  "Timeout"
                ],
                [
                  "Other namespace",
                  "Needs a matching namespaceSelector"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Inspect the policy",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "bash",
              "lines": [
                "kubectl get netpol -n ns",
                "kubectl describe netpol name"
              ],
              "note": "confirm selectors match the intended pods and labels"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Test both an ==allowed== and a ==denied== source",
                "Test from the **right namespace**"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Network Policy Cheat Sheet",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 5,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Network Policy Cheat Sheet",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Defaults and selectors",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "No policy = ==allow all==",
                "Any policy selecting a pod = allow **only what is listed**, per direction",
                "Same list item = {green:AND}; separate items (own dash) = {orange:OR}"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Peer",
                "Matches",
                "Note"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`podSelector: {}`",
                  "all pods in the namespace",
                  "empty = everything"
                ],
                [
                  "`namespaceSelector`",
                  "namespace labels",
                  "label the namespace first"
                ],
                [
                  "`ipBlock`",
                  "CIDR",
                  "optional `except`"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Default deny and DNS",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "yaml",
              "lines": [
                "kind: NetworkPolicy",
                "metadata: {name: default-deny-all}",
                "spec:",
                "  podSelector: {}",
                "  policyTypes: [Ingress, Egress]"
              ],
              "note": "deny all: empty selector, both types, no rules"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Allow DNS: egress to ==kube-dns== (`k8s-app=kube-dns`) on **UDP and TCP 53**",
                "Deny egress without DNS: names fail even when the target IP is allowed; IPs not otherwise allowed are blocked too."
              ],
              "style": "cross"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. CNI and testing",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Needs a policy-aware CNI: {green:Calico} or {green:Cilium}",
                "Flannel alone **silently ignores** policies",
                "Verify with a throwaway busybox pod and `wget --timeout`"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "bash",
              "lines": [
                "kubectl run test --rm -it --image=busybox -- wget -qO- --timeout=2 http://svc:8080"
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Check yourself",
      "role": "quiz",
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Check yourself",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "A namespace has default-deny egress plus a policy allowing egress to `app=db` pods on 5432. `psql -h db-svc` fails, but `psql -h <db-pod-ip>` works. Why?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "Egress deny also blocks **DNS**, so the name never resolves.",
                "Fix: allow egress to kube-dns on UDP and TCP 53."
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "Which sources does this ingress rule allow?",
              "example_code": [
                "from:",
                "- namespaceSelector:",
                "    matchLabels: {team: a}",
                "- podSelector:",
                "    matchLabels: {app: web}"
              ],
              "a_bullets": [
                "Separate items are **OR**: any pod in `team=a` namespaces, or `app=web` pods in the policy's own namespace.",
                "For AND, drop the second dash so both selectors share one item."
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "On a Flannel-only cluster, you apply default-deny, yet another pod still connects. Why?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "Flannel does not enforce policies, so the object is accepted and silently ignored.",
                "Use a policy-aware CNI such as Calico or Cilium."
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}